<article class="env-lemma" id="09SZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09SZ">Lemma <span data-tag="09SZ">20.12.4</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Let $\mathcal{U} : U = \bigcup U_ i$ be an open covering. If $\mathcal{F}$ is flasque, then $\check{H}^ p(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for $p > 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The presheaves $\underline{H}^ q(\mathcal{F})$ used in the statement of Lemma <a href="/tag/01ES" data-tag="01ES">20.11.5</a> are zero by Lemma <a href="/tag/09SY" data-tag="09SY">20.12.3</a>. Hence $\check{H}^ p(U, \mathcal{F}) = H^ p(U, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/09SY" data-tag="09SY">20.12.3</a> again. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>